## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to derive a multi-interval DP with per-interval cost and reconstruction. Requires careful state definition and an O(nk) optimization akin to advanced interval DP.

## Key Concepts

- DP over prefixes and interval counts
- Prefix sums for subarray sums
- Running maximum optimization to avoid O(n^2k)
- Path reconstruction to recover subarray boundaries

## Code Example

```javascript
function maxKSubarrays(A, k, c) {
  const n = A.length;
  const S = Array(n+1).fill(0);
  for (let i=1; i<=n; i++) S[i] = S[i-1] + A[i-1];
  const NEG = -1e15;
  const dp = Array.from({length: n+1}, () => Array(k+1).fill(NEG));
  const prv = Array.from({length: n+1}, () => Array(k+1).fill(-1));
  dp[0][0] = 0;
  for (let t=1; t<=k; t++) {
    let best = NEG;
    for (let i=1; i<=n; i++) {
      const val = dp[i-1][t-1] - S[i-1] + c*(i-1);
      if (val > best) { best = val; }
      const cand = S[i] - c*i + best;
      if (cand > dp[i][t]) { dp[i][t] = cand; prv[i][t] = i; }
      if (dp[i-1][t] > dp[i][t]) { dp[i][t] = dp[i-1][t]; prv[i][t] = -1; }
    }
  }
  // reconstruct (simple backtrack)
  const intervals = [];
  let i = n, t = k;
  while (t > 0 && i > 0) {
    if (prv[i][t] === -1) { i--; continue; }
    const end = i;
    const start = prv[i][t];
    intervals.push([start, end]);
    i = start - 1; t--;
  }
  intervals.reverse();
  return { value: dp[n][k], intervals };
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you extend to allow variable per-interval cost or rewards based on length?
- How would you optimize memory to O(nk) and still reconstruct intervals?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests a fundamental DP pattern with an explicit gap constraint, a natural generalization of the classic non-adjacent selection.

## Key Concepts
- DP over index and remaining picks
- Handling fixed gap via i-g-1 transition
- Space- and time-complexity considerations
- Reconstruction of chosen indices

## Code Example
```javascript
function maxSumWithGap(A, k, g){
  const n = A.length;
  const NEG = -Infinity;
  const dp = Array.from({length: n+1}, ()=> Array(k+1).fill(NEG));
  const prv = Array.from({length: n+1}, ()=> Array(k+1).fill(-1));
  dp[0][0] = 0;
  for(let i=1;i<=n;i++){
    for(let t=0;t<=k;t++){
      // skip
      if(dp[i-1][t] > dp[i][t]){ dp[i][t] = dp[i-1][t]; prv[i][t] = -1; }
      // take i-1
      if(t>0 && i-g-1>=0 && dp[i-g-1][t-1] !== NEG){
        const val = dp[i-g-1][t-1] + A[i-1];
        if(val > dp[i][t]){ dp[i][t] = val; prv[i][t] = i-g-1; }
      }
    }
  }
  // reconstruction omitted for brevity
  return {best: dp[n][k], indices: []};
}
```

